# urllib3 >= 1.26.16 caused deadlocks in uWSGI workers under gevent in
# production, so urllib3 was pinned to 1.26.15
# (https://github.com/hypothesis/viahtml/pull/716). Upstream traced it to
# urllib3's connection pools using a standard library queue, which gevent did
# not monkey-patch, instead of a gevent one. Both projects have since fixed
# that, and these minimum versions make sure we keep both fixes:
#
# - gevent 25.4.1 monkey-patches queue.LifoQueue (and Queue, PriorityQueue)
#   with gevent's cooperative versions:
#   https://github.com/gevent/gevent/issues/1957
# - urllib3 2.8.0 looks up queue.LifoQueue when each connection pool is
#   created, so the patched class is used even if urllib3 was imported before
#   monkey-patching: https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/issues/3289
#
# gevent 25.9.1 is the first release after 25.4.1 that also has the follow-up
# fixes to the new patched queue classes.
gevent>=25.9.1
urllib3>=2.8.0
